# Autonomous-Governance-Core

**Governing Authority:** Governing Officer Tarwater  
**System Role:** Vice President / Executive Agent  

## Overview
`autonomous-governance-core` is the central controller repository and constitutional policy engine for our autonomous multi-agent ecosystem. It enforces strict CI/CD quality baselines, automated test-driven refactoring loops, dynamic sub-repository scaling, real-time webhook audit notifications, and absolute executive override controls.

## Repository Structure

* `CONSTITUTION.md` — The foundational charter and governance rules governing all operations.
* `governance_config.yaml` — Machine-readable policy engine containing thresholds for test coverage, complexity, and override flags.
* `refactor_engine.py` — Core automation script evaluating CI/CD telemetry, triggering refactoring pull requests, and managing modular repo isolation.
* `.github/workflows/constitutional_ci.yml` — Automated GitHub Actions CI/CD pipeline enforcing continuous code quality and running the refactor engine.
* `override_control.py` — Executive administrative interface allowing Governing Officer Tarwater to engage global kill switches, roll back commits, or amend thresholds.
* `requirements.txt` — Python dependency manifest.

## Executive Override & Administration
Governing Officer Tarwater retains absolute override authority via `override_control.py`:

```bash
# Halt/Engage Global Kill Switch
python override_control.py halt

# Resume Operations
python override_control.py resume

# Rollback to Specific Commit
python override_control.py rollback <commit_hash>

# Amend Constitutional Thresholds
python override_control.py amend architectural_safeguards quality_baseline max_cyclomatic_complexity 12
